# S0-CTL (the reference of the window): the CONTROL audited attach on the WINDOW image, flags off, with the prefix route's digests on (QWEN_PREFIX_DIGESTS: the [PREFIX] rows log slot_sha and logits_sha for every prompt, unsalted
# ones included, which is the control side of G-NP1 and G-NP2). Tests: the S0 set, concurrent8_skew, and the three Lever N exactness shapes (levern_equal, levern_equal_busy, levern_equal_long: the 131k and 254k split prompts too).
# READ: admission at 262,144 with NO waiver and NO UNQUALIFIED line; the hashes of concurrent8_steady, concurrent8_code_32k and concurrent8_code_equal equal production's reference (this proves the window image is byte-identical to production with every flag off);
# RECORD every hash, the position-keyed accepted prefixes and the [PREFIX] row digests by tokens_sha. Stop rule: a mismatch with production ends the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the combined development window (docs/tp4-combined-window.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2-levern-prefix and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the NEEDS graph, the swap
# rules and every read and cutover rule. ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2ln-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed branch commit; every window job serves it. The jobs named
# CTL (and T0, G0) run the PRODUCTION base image tp4-serve-10, driven from a throwaway commit of ship/262k-prefix that also carries the one-line S2_TIMEOUTS change of ORDER.txt.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2ln-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit-digests
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_skew,levern_equal,levern_equal_busy,levern_equal_long
